<?xml version="1.0" encoding="ISO-8859-1"?>
<wps:ProcessDescriptions xmlns:wps="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0" xmlns:ows="http://www.opengis.net/ows/1.1" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0 schemas/wps/1.0.0/wpsDescribeProcess_response.xsd" service="WPS" version="1.0.0" xml:lang="en-US">
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:Vecselec:COND1_CAMP</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>Query Mode</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>In this mode a query is made of the database and all the graphical objects satisfying the condition are selected. The query may be made up of up to 100 simple queries linked by 'and' or 'or'. Each query may be based on any of the database fields using numerical or alphanumeric operators. To obtain more information on the values of parameters that define the selection follow the guidelines in the <![CDATA[<a href="general.htm#SelecAtrib">general syntax</a>]]> document.</ows:Abstract>
		<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Title:Selection of a subset of vector entities"/>
		<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Abstract:This application selects a subset of graphical objects, whether points, arcs, nodes, polygons or groups of polygons, from one file and copies them to a second file in the same format. In the case of nodes, the selected subset is stored in a points file since it is not possible to generate a new node layer without their corresponding arcs."/>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerTOPOri</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Input TOP file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the name of the topological file from which the selection is made based on a query with optional parameters.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:InputTOPfile"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pnt</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pnt</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-arc</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pol</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-nod</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/octet-stream</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-rel</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="100">
				<ows:Identifier>COND#_FIELD</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Field of Condition #</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Field name of # condition of selection. It may be made up to 100 simple queries and 100 field names (COND#_CAMP) starting at index 1.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="100">
				<ows:Identifier>COND#_OP</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Operation of condition #</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Opertation of # condition of selection. It may be made up to 100 simple queries and 100 operations (COND#_OP) starting at index 1.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>EQ</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>NO_EQ</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>LT</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>GT</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>LT_EQ</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>GT_EQ</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>INTERVAL</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="99">
				<ows:Identifier>COND#_NEXE</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Nexus linking of condition #</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Nexus use to linking for the successive selections. In this case to linking between condition # and condition #+1. It may be made up to 100 simple queries and 99 nexus (COND#_NEXE) starting at index 1.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>AND</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>OR</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="100">
				<ows:Identifier>COND#_VALOR</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Value of condition #</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Value of # condition of selection. It may be made up to 100 simple queries and 100 values (COND#_VALOR) starting at index 1.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>NO_POLZERO</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>NO_POLZERO</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>The application will not generate the description of the polygon 0 and the resulting polygon file will be marked as a topological group.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>SOBRESCRIURE</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>SOBRESCRIURE</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>If output file exist overwrite it. By default the application adds selected objects to preexisting ones in output file if both hve the same structure.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>AGRUPA_NO_SELEC</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>AGRUPA_NO_SELEC</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Unselected inner objects are grouped to 0 polygon. By default inner objects are created thematic attributes but this polygons can be tricky when you analize de area of results.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>EMANCIPA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>EMANCIPA</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>In polygon selection, it means that output polygon file will be emancipated from intput arc source.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerTOP</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>TOP file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the name of the topological file into which the selected objects are copied. The type of output file is dependent on the input file.
				</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:TOPFile"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pnt</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pnt</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-arc</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pol</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-nod</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:Vecselec:!COND1_CAMP</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>List Mode</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract>A text file indicates which are the graphic entities and the database records  to be saved in the output file. </ows:Abstract>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerSEL</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>SEL file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the name of the selection file.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:SELfile"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-sel</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-sel</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>text/plain</MimeType>
							<Encoding>ascii</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>NO_POLZERO</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>NO_POLZERO</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>The application will not generate the description of the polygon 0 and the resulting polygon file will be marked as a topological group.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>SOBRESCRIURE</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>SOBRESCRIURE</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>If output file exist overwrite it. By default the application adds selected objects to preexisting ones in output file if both hve the same structure.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>AGRUPA_NO_SELEC</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>AGRUPA_NO_SELEC</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Unselected inner objects are grouped to 0 polygon. By default inner objects are created thematic attributes but this polygons can be tricky when you analize de area of results.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>EMANCIPA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>EMANCIPA</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>In polygon selection, it means that output polygon file will be emancipated from intput arc source.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerTOP</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>TOP file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the name of the topological file into which the selected objects are copied. The type of output file is dependent on the input file.
				</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:TOPFile"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pnt</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pnt</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-arc</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-pol</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-nod</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
</wps:ProcessDescriptions>
